1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,374
This is the Corsair Queen,

2
00:00:01,824 --> 00:00:03,767
and she isn't in the game you installed.

3
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:07,796
I wrote her this morning, in one small text file,

4
00:00:08,246 --> 00:00:10,318
and I didn't write any code to do it.

5
00:00:12,118 --> 00:00:13,344
By the end of this lecture,

6
00:00:13,794 --> 00:00:16,554
you'll have a boss of your own in that list.

7
00:00:17,754 --> 00:00:20,384
You played Siege in the very first lecture.

8
00:00:21,284 --> 00:00:23,194
Raiders come at your starbases,

9
00:00:23,644 --> 00:00:26,043
and you win when the last raider is gone.

10
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:28,997
Now, if you choose a boss,

11
00:00:29,447 --> 00:00:33,066
something worse arrives when the raiders are nearly beaten.

12
00:00:34,866 --> 00:00:36,571
Four bosses come with the game,

13
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:39,849
and each one is a single file in a folder.

14
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:43,170
So if you add a file, you've added a boss.

15
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:47,270
Before we open his file, here's the Warlord in the game.

16
00:00:48,170 --> 00:00:49,954
He's a name in the Boss list,

17
00:00:50,404 --> 00:00:53,574
and when he arrives, his flagship shows on Science,

18
00:00:54,024 --> 00:00:55,289
with his name at the top.

19
00:00:56,189 --> 00:01:01,773
And his objective, Defeat the Warlord, is in the Quest Log on Helm's handheld.

20
00:01:03,573 --> 00:01:05,984
Here's his file, and it's two records,

21
00:01:06,434 --> 00:01:07,999
in the shape you already know:

22
00:01:08,449 --> 00:01:11,388
a heading, a fence, and a body.

23
00:01:12,288 --> 00:01:14,690
The first record is the boss himself,

24
00:01:15,140 --> 00:01:18,179
and the name in its heading is the one in the Boss list.

25
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:22,033
There's one word alone on a line, the word Boss,

26
00:01:22,483 --> 00:01:25,229
which says what kind of record this is.

27
00:01:26,129 --> 00:01:28,382
Trigger and Low say when he arrives:

28
00:01:28,832 --> 00:01:30,912
when a quarter of the raiders are left.

29
00:01:31,812 --> 00:01:34,294
Flies and Fleets say what comes with him,

30
00:01:34,744 --> 00:01:36,633
and Named is his flagship:

31
00:01:37,083 --> 00:01:39,225
a name, and then which ship it is.

32
00:01:41,025 --> 00:01:43,009
The second record is a quest,

33
00:01:43,459 --> 00:01:45,316
and it's the one in the Quest Log.

34
00:01:46,216 --> 00:01:48,581
You wrote plenty of those in Class 1.

35
00:01:49,481 --> 00:01:51,475
It belongs to the Siege's own mission,

36
00:01:51,925 --> 00:01:53,623
the crew needs it to win,

37
00:01:54,073 --> 00:01:57,849
and it's done when the Siege says every raider is gone.

38
00:01:59,049 --> 00:02:00,857
Don't edit the Warlord. Copy it.

39
00:02:01,757 --> 00:02:04,753
And don't paste it back into the game's own folder,

40
00:02:05,203 --> 00:02:08,958
because that folder is replaced every time the game is updated.

41
00:02:09,858 --> 00:02:12,831
Yours goes here instead, in common data,

42
00:02:13,281 --> 00:02:15,580
and then a folder called bosses.

43
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,325
The Siege reads both folders,

44
00:02:19,775 --> 00:02:22,707
so a file in either one is a boss in the list.

45
00:02:23,607 --> 00:02:27,246
For the file's name, use small letters and underscores,

46
00:02:27,696 --> 00:02:29,221
and leave out the spaces.

47
00:02:30,421 --> 00:02:32,940
Before I change anything, I'm going to run lint,

48
00:02:33,390 --> 00:02:35,230
pointed at my own bosses folder.

49
00:02:36,130 --> 00:02:38,184
And it already has something to say.

50
00:02:39,084 --> 00:02:41,361
My copy still has the Warlord's name,

51
00:02:41,812 --> 00:02:43,874
and the list offers bosses by name,

52
00:02:44,324 --> 00:02:46,297
so only one of the two can be in it.

53
00:02:48,097 --> 00:02:51,113
It's a true warning, and it's the first thing we'll fix.

54
00:02:52,313 --> 00:02:55,619
The square brackets hold the name the Boss list shows,

55
00:02:56,069 --> 00:02:57,948
and the round brackets hold the key,

56
00:02:58,398 --> 00:03:00,462
which I make the same as my file's name.

57
00:03:01,362 --> 00:03:02,813
Next is her flagship,

58
00:03:03,263 --> 00:03:06,671
the name Science shows at the top when she's selected,

59
00:03:07,121 --> 00:03:10,200
and I'm only changing the first word, the ship's name.

60
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,857
There's one trap here, and it catches people.

61
00:03:15,757 --> 00:03:18,680
A flagship's name has to be one word.

62
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:22,592
If I type Iron Duke, as two words,

63
00:03:23,042 --> 00:03:24,977
the game reads a ship called Iron,

64
00:03:25,427 --> 00:03:26,758
of a kind called Duke,

65
00:03:27,208 --> 00:03:29,250
and there's no such kind of ship.

66
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:31,777
Lint does catch that one,

67
00:03:32,227 --> 00:03:35,019
and it shows you the line to write instead.

68
00:03:36,219 --> 00:03:37,660
Now for the part you're here for.

69
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:41,274
Under the first fence goes one line about her.

70
00:03:42,174 --> 00:03:46,163
That one's a note for you, and for anyone you give the file to,

71
00:03:46,613 --> 00:03:48,399
because the game doesn't show it to the crew.

72
00:03:49,299 --> 00:03:52,516
The objective is different, since the crew reads it in the Quest Log,

73
00:03:52,966 --> 00:03:54,663
the way they read the Warlord's.

74
00:03:55,563 --> 00:03:58,071
So it gets a new name, a new key,

75
00:03:58,521 --> 00:04:01,424
what it pays, and a sentence in your own voice.

76
00:04:03,224 --> 00:04:05,793
Leave the five lines in the middle alone today,

77
00:04:06,243 --> 00:04:10,367
and keep the word credits after the number, or nothing gets paid.

78
00:04:11,267 --> 00:04:13,457
Then save, run lint again,

79
00:04:13,907 --> 00:04:16,391
and this time it says clean.

80
00:04:17,591 --> 00:04:21,175
To see her, I start the game the way you have since Class 1,

81
00:04:21,625 --> 00:04:24,538
but with Legendary Missions as the mission,

82
00:04:24,988 --> 00:04:27,679
and with no map on the end of the line.

83
00:04:28,579 --> 00:04:30,890
That leaves the server on the start screen.

84
00:04:31,790 --> 00:04:33,057
Siege is on the left,

85
00:04:33,507 --> 00:04:37,386
and on the right is the Options panel, with a line called Boss.

86
00:04:39,186 --> 00:04:41,622
And there she is, at the top of the list,

87
00:04:42,072 --> 00:04:43,662
above the game's own four.

88
00:04:44,562 --> 00:04:45,952
If she's missing for you,

89
00:04:46,402 --> 00:04:47,936
the file's in the wrong folder,

90
00:04:48,386 --> 00:04:50,883
or the game was already running when you saved it.

91
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:56,520
At twenty-five percent, you'd fight for a long time before she showed up.

92
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,726
So for testing, I set Low to ninety.

93
00:05:00,626 --> 00:05:03,925
Now she comes when one raider in ten is gone,

94
00:05:04,375 --> 00:05:06,271
which here is after the second kill.

95
00:05:08,071 --> 00:05:10,042
There's the Morrigan on Science,

96
00:05:10,492 --> 00:05:12,345
her name in red at the top,

97
00:05:12,795 --> 00:05:13,669
among the raiders.

98
00:05:14,569 --> 00:05:19,897
And on Helm's handheld, there's my objective in the Quest Log, in my words.

99
00:05:20,797 --> 00:05:22,438
Notice that nothing announced her.

100
00:05:22,888 --> 00:05:25,519
The game doesn't tell the crew a boss has arrived,

101
00:05:25,969 --> 00:05:28,209
and we'll do something about that later in the class.

102
00:05:29,109 --> 00:05:32,380
When you've finished testing, put Low back to twenty-five.

103
00:05:33,580 --> 00:05:35,294
This is why she lives out here.

104
00:05:36,194 --> 00:05:37,682
You can update the game,

105
00:05:38,132 --> 00:05:39,923
and this folder is left alone.

106
00:05:40,823 --> 00:05:43,368
It's still one file on one computer, though,

107
00:05:43,818 --> 00:05:45,651
so keep a copy somewhere else,

108
00:05:46,101 --> 00:05:48,195
the way you would with a manuscript.

109
00:05:49,995 --> 00:05:53,717
And to give her to a friend, you send them that one file.

110
00:05:54,617 --> 00:05:56,975
Now make a second boss, from your own story.

111
00:05:57,875 --> 00:06:00,351
Next time, we change the numbers.
